% ============================================================================
% triangle-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the geometry triangle-types
% library (triangles classified BY THEIR SIDES).
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what makes a triangle
% isosceles?": it states no geometry fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `triangle_sides` rows and returns the side-condition + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the condition
% `three_equal_sides`, recall its type — equilateral). A word that is not one of
% the three side-classes abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% condition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli triangle-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "triangle-types.adj"

? triangle_sides(equilateral, $Condition)   % expect three_equal_sides
? triangle_sides(isosceles, $Condition)     % expect two_equal_sides
? triangle_sides(scalene, $Condition)       % expect three_unequal_sides
? triangle_sides($Type, three_equal_sides)  % reverse bind — expect equilateral
? triangle_sides(square, $Condition)        % expect abstain — a square is not a triangle
